# __PROJECT__

C++__CPP_STANDARD__ console starter using MSVC x64, CMake 3.28+ and Ninja.
Use VS Code, Neovim or Visual Studio. Install the compiler/Windows SDK and CMake/Ninja;
the build helper discovers an existing C++ installation and does not install tools.

```powershell
./scripts/Build.ps1
./build/dev/bin/__PROJECT__.exe
./scripts/Build.ps1 -Configuration Release
```

Or run `./scripts/Enter-DevShell.ps1`, then use the CMake `dev`/`release` presets directly.
An editor launched from that shell inherits the environment. Configure editor diagnostics
from `build/dev/compile_commands.json` instead of maintaining a second set of flags.

The initial target uses the dynamic MSVC CRT, exceptions, and warnings as errors for owned
code. Record the actual compiler and SDK versions after building. C++23 may map to
`/std:c++latest` in a particular CMake/MSVC pairing; inspect the actual compiler command.
Choose and test runtime/deployment settings when the application gains consumers.

Add reusable logic as library targets and add meaningful tests when behavior exists.
`./scripts/Build.ps1 -Test` runs CTest and fails while no tests are defined.
`-Fresh` reconfigures after a toolchain change. Use separate build directories/presets for
different architectures or generators. Formatting/analysis files are included only when
existing configurations were supplied to the generator.
